---
title: World Generation
id: world-generation
order: 7
description: "Generate a world with generateWorld(). Live adapters mint a session token. Job adapters return a finished 3D world URL."
keywords:
  - tanstack ai
  - world generation
  - generateWorld
  - reactor
  - worldlabs
  - marble
  - orbis
  - infinite world
  - live video
  - experimental
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You want a world from a prompt. Some providers open a live session you can steer. Other providers generate a finished 3D world. Open "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"world.url"},{"type":"text","value":" to view it. Asset URLs on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"world.assets"},{"type":"text","value":" are often signed."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateWorld()"},{"type":"text","value":" on the server with a world adapter. Reactor mints a session token. World Labs returns a Marble viewer URL after the job finishes."}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Experimental."}]},{"type":"text","value":" The API can change. Live world models bill per session-second while a GPU is held. World Labs bills in credits per generation."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"1-mint-a-session-on-the-server","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1. Mint a session on the server"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The browser can paste a Reactor key. The relay reads "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x-byok-reactor"},{"type":"text","value":", then "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"REACTOR_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":". Do not put the key in the JSON body."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateWorld } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { byokMissing, getByokKey } from '@tanstack/ai/byok/server'\nimport { reactorWorld } from '@tanstack/ai-reactor'\nimport { reactorByok } from '@tanstack/ai-reactor/byok'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const apiKey = getByokKey(request, reactorByok)\n  if (!apiKey) return byokMissing(reactorByok)\n\n  const body = await request.json()\n  const prompt = typeof body.prompt === 'string' ? body.prompt : ''\n  if (prompt.length === 0) {\n    return Response.json({ error: 'prompt is required' }, { status: 400 })\n  }\n\n  const world = await generateWorld({\n    adapter: reactorWorld('visko-orbis-stable', { apiKey }),\n    prompt,\n  })\n\n  return Response.json({\n    token: world.token,\n    model: world.model,\n    prompt: world.prompt,\n    expiresAt: world.expiresAt,\n  })\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See "},{"type":"link","href":"../advanced/byok","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Bring Your Own Key"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for the client store."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"2-connect-in-the-browser","children":[{"type":"text","value":"2. Connect in the browser"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Install "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@reactor-team/js-sdk"},{"type":"text","value":". Connect with the token. Then set the prompt and start."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { Reactor } from '@reactor-team/js-sdk'\nimport { defineByok, defaultByokStorage } from '@tanstack/ai-client/byok'\nimport { reactorByok } from '@tanstack/ai-reactor/byok'\n\nconst byok = defineByok({\n  storage: defaultByokStorage(),\n  providers: [reactorByok],\n})\nbyok.setServerCoverage(true)\n\nconst video = document.querySelector('video')\nif (!video) {\n  throw new Error('Missing video element')\n}\n\nconst world = await fetch('/api/world', {\n  method: 'POST',\n  headers: {\n    'Content-Type': 'application/json',\n    ...byok.headers(reactorByok.id),\n  },\n  body: JSON.stringify({\n    prompt:\n      'A dramatic coastline of black volcanic cliffs at golden hour, a single unbroken take.',\n  }),\n}).then(async (response) => {\n  if (!response.ok) {\n    throw new Error('World session failed')\n  }\n  return response.json()\n})\n\nconst token = typeof world.token === 'string' ? world.token : ''\nconst model = typeof world.model === 'string' ? world.model : ''\nconst prompt = typeof world.prompt === 'string' ? world.prompt : ''\nif (token.length === 0 || model.length === 0 || prompt.length === 0) {\n  throw new Error('World payload is incomplete')\n}\n\nconst reactor = new Reactor({ modelName: model })\n\nreactor.on('trackReceived', (name, _track, stream) => {\n  if (name !== 'main_video') return\n  video.muted = true\n  const attach = () => {\n    video.srcObject = null\n    video.srcObject = stream\n    void video.play().catch((error: unknown) => {\n      if (error instanceof DOMException && error.name === 'AbortError') return\n    })\n  }\n  attach()\n  for (const track of stream.getTracks()) {\n    track.addEventListener('unmute', attach)\n  }\n})\n\nawait reactor.connect(token)\nawait reactor.sendCommand('set_resolution', { resolution: '1080p' })\nawait reactor.sendCommand('set_prompt', { prompt })\nawait reactor.sendCommand('start', {})","lang":"ts","meta":"group=world-browser"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The video element now plays a live world. A new "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"set_prompt"},{"type":"text","value":" during the run morphs the scene at the next chunk."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"LingBot and LingBot World 2 start from a seed image. Pass a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"File"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<input type=\"file\" accept=\"image/png,image/jpeg\">"},{"type":"text","value":". The SDK uploads the file. Do not send base64. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"start"},{"type":"text","value":" also needs "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"set_prompt"},{"type":"text","value":". Write the prompt to describe what the image shows. When the prompt and the image disagree, the image wins and the world drifts."}]},{"type":"code","value":"const picker = document.querySelector('input[type=\"file\"]')\nif (!(picker instanceof HTMLInputElement)) {\n  throw new Error('Pick a seed image')\n}\nconst file = picker.files?.[0]\nif (file === undefined) {\n  throw new Error('Pick a seed image')\n}\nconst image = await reactor.uploadFile(file)\nawait reactor.sendCommand('set_image', { image })\nawait reactor.sendCommand('set_prompt', { prompt })\nawait reactor.sendCommand('start', {})","lang":"ts","meta":"group=world-browser"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"models","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Models"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reactorWorld()"},{"type":"text","value":" accepts these ids. The result "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"model"},{"type":"text","value":" field is the Reactor connect slug."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Id"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Connect slug"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What it does"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"visko-orbis-stable"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reactor/visko-orbis-stable"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Steerable video with realtime audio"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"visko-orbis-dynamic"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reactor/visko-orbis-dynamic"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Same family, live resolution switch"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lingbot-world-2"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reactor/lingbot-world-2"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Image-anchored navigable world"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lingbot"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reactor/lingbot"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Image-anchored navigable video"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"helios"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reactor/helios"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Interactive realtime video"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Happy Oyster ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"happy-oyster-adventure"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"happy-oyster-director"},{"type":"text","value":") uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createWorld"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"startTravel"},{"type":"text","value":" after connect. See the "},{"type":"link","href":"../adapters/reactor","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reactor adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for every id. Helios also works with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateLiveVideo()"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reactorVideo()"},{"type":"text","value":". See "},{"type":"link","href":"./live-generation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Live Generation"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A full app lives in "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/tree/main/examples/ts-react-media","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"examples/ts-react-media"}]},{"type":"text","value":". Open the World tab. Pick a Reactor model for a live stream, or a Marble model for a finished 3D world. If splat files are present, the example loads one SPZ in Spark. If not, it shows a thumbnail and an Open in Marble link."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"finished-3d-worlds-world-labs","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Finished 3D worlds (World Labs)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"World Labs Marble is a job, not a live stream. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateWorld()"},{"type":"text","value":" waits until the world is ready, then returns a viewer URL and asset links."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateWorld } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { worldlabsWorld } from '@tanstack/ai-worldlabs'\n\nconst world = await generateWorld({\n  adapter: worldlabsWorld('marble-1.1'),\n  prompt: 'A mystical forest with glowing mushrooms',\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"world.url"},{"type":"text","value":" is the Marble viewer. Do not iframe it. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"world.assets"},{"type":"text","value":" is optional and holds splat, mesh, and panorama URLs when the provider returns them. See the "},{"type":"link","href":"../adapters/worldlabs","children":[{"type":"text","value":"World Labs adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for image and video inputs, models, and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"wait: false"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"wait: false"},{"type":"text","value":" returns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"operationId"},{"type":"text","value":". This SDK cannot resume that id."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"what-you-have-now","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What you have now"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A server route that mints a live world session, or a server call that returns a finished Marble world. For Reactor, connect in the browser and change the prompt to steer the stream. The media example can save a Reactor session as MP4 when recording is enabled for that model or plan, and download Marble files when the response includes them."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"1-mint-a-session-on-the-server","text":"1. Mint a session on the server","level":2},{"id":"2-connect-in-the-browser","text":"2. Connect in the browser","level":2},{"id":"models","text":"Models","level":2},{"id":"finished-3d-worlds-world-labs","text":"Finished 3D worlds (World Labs)","level":2},{"id":"what-you-have-now","text":"What you have now","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nYou want a world from a prompt. Some providers open a live session you can steer. Other providers generate a finished 3D world. Open `world.url` to view it. Asset URLs on `world.assets` are often signed.\n\nCall `generateWorld()` on the server with a world adapter. Reactor mints a session token. World Labs returns a Marble viewer URL after the job finishes.\n\n> **Experimental.** The API can change. Live world models bill per session-second while a GPU is held. World Labs bills in credits per generation.\n\n## 1. Mint a session on the server\n\nThe browser can paste a Reactor key. The relay reads `x-byok-reactor`, then `REACTOR_API_KEY`. Do not put the key in the JSON body.\n\n```ts\nimport { generateWorld } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { byokMissing, getByokKey } from '@tanstack/ai/byok/server'\nimport { reactorWorld } from '@tanstack/ai-reactor'\nimport { reactorByok } from '@tanstack/ai-reactor/byok'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const apiKey = getByokKey(request, reactorByok)\n  if (!apiKey) return byokMissing(reactorByok)\n\n  const body = await request.json()\n  const prompt = typeof body.prompt === 'string' ? body.prompt : ''\n  if (prompt.length === 0) {\n    return Response.json({ error: 'prompt is required' }, { status: 400 })\n  }\n\n  const world = await generateWorld({\n    adapter: reactorWorld('visko-orbis-stable', { apiKey }),\n    prompt,\n  })\n\n  return Response.json({\n    token: world.token,\n    model: world.model,\n    prompt: world.prompt,\n    expiresAt: world.expiresAt,\n  })\n}\n```\n\nSee [Bring Your Own Key](../advanced/byok) for the client store.\n\n## 2. Connect in the browser\n\nInstall `@reactor-team/js-sdk`. Connect with the token. Then set the prompt and start.\n\n```ts group=world-browser\nimport { Reactor } from '@reactor-team/js-sdk'\nimport { defineByok, defaultByokStorage } from '@tanstack/ai-client/byok'\nimport { reactorByok } from '@tanstack/ai-reactor/byok'\n\nconst byok = defineByok({\n  storage: defaultByokStorage(),\n  providers: [reactorByok],\n})\nbyok.setServerCoverage(true)\n\nconst video = document.querySelector('video')\nif (!video) {\n  throw new Error('Missing video element')\n}\n\nconst world = await fetch('/api/world', {\n  method: 'POST',\n  headers: {\n    'Content-Type': 'application/json',\n    ...byok.headers(reactorByok.id),\n  },\n  body: JSON.stringify({\n    prompt:\n      'A dramatic coastline of black volcanic cliffs at golden hour, a single unbroken take.',\n  }),\n}).then(async (response) => {\n  if (!response.ok) {\n    throw new Error('World session failed')\n  }\n  return response.json()\n})\n\nconst token = typeof world.token === 'string' ? world.token : ''\nconst model = typeof world.model === 'string' ? world.model : ''\nconst prompt = typeof world.prompt === 'string' ? world.prompt : ''\nif (token.length === 0 || model.length === 0 || prompt.length === 0) {\n  throw new Error('World payload is incomplete')\n}\n\nconst reactor = new Reactor({ modelName: model })\n\nreactor.on('trackReceived', (name, _track, stream) => {\n  if (name !== 'main_video') return\n  video.muted = true\n  const attach = () => {\n    video.srcObject = null\n    video.srcObject = stream\n    void video.play().catch((error: unknown) => {\n      if (error instanceof DOMException && error.name === 'AbortError') return\n    })\n  }\n  attach()\n  for (const track of stream.getTracks()) {\n    track.addEventListener('unmute', attach)\n  }\n})\n\nawait reactor.connect(token)\nawait reactor.sendCommand('set_resolution', { resolution: '1080p' })\nawait reactor.sendCommand('set_prompt', { prompt })\nawait reactor.sendCommand('start', {})\n```\n\nThe video element now plays a live world. A new `set_prompt` during the run morphs the scene at the next chunk.\n\nLingBot and LingBot World 2 start from a seed image. Pass a `File` from `<input type=\"file\" accept=\"image/png,image/jpeg\">`. The SDK uploads the file. Do not send base64. `start` also needs `set_prompt`. Write the prompt to describe what the image shows. When the prompt and the image disagree, the image wins and the world drifts.\n\n```ts group=world-browser\nconst picker = document.querySelector('input[type=\"file\"]')\nif (!(picker instanceof HTMLInputElement)) {\n  throw new Error('Pick a seed image')\n}\nconst file = picker.files?.[0]\nif (file === undefined) {\n  throw new Error('Pick a seed image')\n}\nconst image = await reactor.uploadFile(file)\nawait reactor.sendCommand('set_image', { image })\nawait reactor.sendCommand('set_prompt', { prompt })\nawait reactor.sendCommand('start', {})\n```\n\n## Models\n\n`reactorWorld()` accepts these ids. The result `model` field is the Reactor connect slug.\n\n| Id | Connect slug | What it does |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `visko-orbis-stable` | `reactor/visko-orbis-stable` | Steerable video with realtime audio |\n| `visko-orbis-dynamic` | `reactor/visko-orbis-dynamic` | Same family, live resolution switch |\n| `lingbot-world-2` | `reactor/lingbot-world-2` | Image-anchored navigable world |\n| `lingbot` | `reactor/lingbot` | Image-anchored navigable video |\n| `helios` | `reactor/helios` | Interactive realtime video |\n\nHappy Oyster (`happy-oyster-adventure`, `happy-oyster-director`) uses `createWorld` and `startTravel` after connect. See the [Reactor adapter](../adapters/reactor) for every id. Helios also works with `generateLiveVideo()` and `reactorVideo()`. See [Live Generation](./live-generation).\n\nA full app lives in [`examples/ts-react-media`](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/tree/main/examples/ts-react-media). Open the World tab. Pick a Reactor model for a live stream, or a Marble model for a finished 3D world. If splat files are present, the example loads one SPZ in Spark. If not, it shows a thumbnail and an Open in Marble link.\n\n## Finished 3D worlds (World Labs)\n\nWorld Labs Marble is a job, not a live stream. `generateWorld()` waits until the world is ready, then returns a viewer URL and asset links.\n\n```ts\nimport { generateWorld } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { worldlabsWorld } from '@tanstack/ai-worldlabs'\n\nconst world = await generateWorld({\n  adapter: worldlabsWorld('marble-1.1'),\n  prompt: 'A mystical forest with glowing mushrooms',\n})\n```\n\n`world.url` is the Marble viewer. Do not iframe it. `world.assets` is optional and holds splat, mesh, and panorama URLs when the provider returns them. See the [World Labs adapter](../adapters/worldlabs) for image and video inputs, models, and `wait: false`. `wait: false` returns `operationId`. This SDK cannot resume that id.\n\n## What you have now\n\nA server route that mints a live world session, or a server call that returns a finished Marble world. For Reactor, connect in the browser and change the prompt to steer the stream. The media example can save a Reactor session as MP4 when recording is enabled for that model or plan, and download Marble files when the response includes them.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: World Generation\nid: world-generation\norder: 7\ndescription: \"Generate a world with generateWorld(). Live adapters mint a session token. Job adapters return a finished 3D world URL.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - world generation\n  - generateWorld\n  - reactor\n  - worldlabs\n  - marble\n  - orbis\n  - infinite world\n  - live video\n  - experimental\n---\n\nYou want a world from a prompt. Some providers open a live session you can steer. Other providers generate a finished 3D world. Open `world.url` to view it. Asset URLs on `world.assets` are often signed.\n\nCall `generateWorld()` on the server with a world adapter. Reactor mints a session token. World Labs returns a Marble viewer URL after the job finishes.\n\n> **Experimental.** The API can change. Live world models bill per session-second while a GPU is held. World Labs bills in credits per generation.\n\n## 1. Mint a session on the server\n\nThe browser can paste a Reactor key. The relay reads `x-byok-reactor`, then `REACTOR_API_KEY`. Do not put the key in the JSON body.\n\n```ts\nimport { generateWorld } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { byokMissing, getByokKey } from '@tanstack/ai/byok/server'\nimport { reactorWorld } from '@tanstack/ai-reactor'\nimport { reactorByok } from '@tanstack/ai-reactor/byok'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const apiKey = getByokKey(request, reactorByok)\n  if (!apiKey) return byokMissing(reactorByok)\n\n  const body = await request.json()\n  const prompt = typeof body.prompt === 'string' ? body.prompt : ''\n  if (prompt.length === 0) {\n    return Response.json({ error: 'prompt is required' }, { status: 400 })\n  }\n\n  const world = await generateWorld({\n    adapter: reactorWorld('visko-orbis-stable', { apiKey }),\n    prompt,\n  })\n\n  return Response.json({\n    token: world.token,\n    model: world.model,\n    prompt: world.prompt,\n    expiresAt: world.expiresAt,\n  })\n}\n```\n\nSee [Bring Your Own Key](../advanced/byok) for the client store.\n\n## 2. Connect in the browser\n\nInstall `@reactor-team/js-sdk`. Connect with the token. Then set the prompt and start.\n\n```ts group=world-browser\nimport { Reactor } from '@reactor-team/js-sdk'\nimport { defineByok, defaultByokStorage } from '@tanstack/ai-client/byok'\nimport { reactorByok } from '@tanstack/ai-reactor/byok'\n\nconst byok = defineByok({\n  storage: defaultByokStorage(),\n  providers: [reactorByok],\n})\nbyok.setServerCoverage(true)\n\nconst video = document.querySelector('video')\nif (!video) {\n  throw new Error('Missing video element')\n}\n\nconst world = await fetch('/api/world', {\n  method: 'POST',\n  headers: {\n    'Content-Type': 'application/json',\n    ...byok.headers(reactorByok.id),\n  },\n  body: JSON.stringify({\n    prompt:\n      'A dramatic coastline of black volcanic cliffs at golden hour, a single unbroken take.',\n  }),\n}).then(async (response) => {\n  if (!response.ok) {\n    throw new Error('World session failed')\n  }\n  return response.json()\n})\n\nconst token = typeof world.token === 'string' ? world.token : ''\nconst model = typeof world.model === 'string' ? world.model : ''\nconst prompt = typeof world.prompt === 'string' ? world.prompt : ''\nif (token.length === 0 || model.length === 0 || prompt.length === 0) {\n  throw new Error('World payload is incomplete')\n}\n\nconst reactor = new Reactor({ modelName: model })\n\nreactor.on('trackReceived', (name, _track, stream) => {\n  if (name !== 'main_video') return\n  video.muted = true\n  const attach = () => {\n    video.srcObject = null\n    video.srcObject = stream\n    void video.play().catch((error: unknown) => {\n      if (error instanceof DOMException && error.name === 'AbortError') return\n    })\n  }\n  attach()\n  for (const track of stream.getTracks()) {\n    track.addEventListener('unmute', attach)\n  }\n})\n\nawait reactor.connect(token)\nawait reactor.sendCommand('set_resolution', { resolution: '1080p' })\nawait reactor.sendCommand('set_prompt', { prompt })\nawait reactor.sendCommand('start', {})\n```\n\nThe video element now plays a live world. A new `set_prompt` during the run morphs the scene at the next chunk.\n\nLingBot and LingBot World 2 start from a seed image. Pass a `File` from `<input type=\"file\" accept=\"image/png,image/jpeg\">`. The SDK uploads the file. Do not send base64. `start` also needs `set_prompt`. Write the prompt to describe what the image shows. When the prompt and the image disagree, the image wins and the world drifts.\n\n```ts group=world-browser\nconst picker = document.querySelector('input[type=\"file\"]')\nif (!(picker instanceof HTMLInputElement)) {\n  throw new Error('Pick a seed image')\n}\nconst file = picker.files?.[0]\nif (file === undefined) {\n  throw new Error('Pick a seed image')\n}\nconst image = await reactor.uploadFile(file)\nawait reactor.sendCommand('set_image', { image })\nawait reactor.sendCommand('set_prompt', { prompt })\nawait reactor.sendCommand('start', {})\n```\n\n## Models\n\n`reactorWorld()` accepts these ids. The result `model` field is the Reactor connect slug.\n\n| Id | Connect slug | What it does |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `visko-orbis-stable` | `reactor/visko-orbis-stable` | Steerable video with realtime audio |\n| `visko-orbis-dynamic` | `reactor/visko-orbis-dynamic` | Same family, live resolution switch |\n| `lingbot-world-2` | `reactor/lingbot-world-2` | Image-anchored navigable world |\n| `lingbot` | `reactor/lingbot` | Image-anchored navigable video |\n| `helios` | `reactor/helios` | Interactive realtime video |\n\nHappy Oyster (`happy-oyster-adventure`, `happy-oyster-director`) uses `createWorld` and `startTravel` after connect. See the [Reactor adapter](../adapters/reactor) for every id. Helios also works with `generateLiveVideo()` and `reactorVideo()`. See [Live Generation](./live-generation).\n\nA full app lives in [`examples/ts-react-media`](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/tree/main/examples/ts-react-media). Open the World tab. Pick a Reactor model for a live stream, or a Marble model for a finished 3D world. If splat files are present, the example loads one SPZ in Spark. If not, it shows a thumbnail and an Open in Marble link.\n\n## Finished 3D worlds (World Labs)\n\nWorld Labs Marble is a job, not a live stream. `generateWorld()` waits until the world is ready, then returns a viewer URL and asset links.\n\n```ts\nimport { generateWorld } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { worldlabsWorld } from '@tanstack/ai-worldlabs'\n\nconst world = await generateWorld({\n  adapter: worldlabsWorld('marble-1.1'),\n  prompt: 'A mystical forest with glowing mushrooms',\n})\n```\n\n`world.url` is the Marble viewer. Do not iframe it. `world.assets` is optional and holds splat, mesh, and panorama URLs when the provider returns them. See the [World Labs adapter](../adapters/worldlabs) for image and video inputs, models, and `wait: false`. `wait: false` returns `operationId`. This SDK cannot resume that id.\n\n## What you have now\n\nA server route that mints a live world session, or a server call that returns a finished Marble world. For Reactor, connect in the browser and change the prompt to steer the stream. The media example can save a Reactor session as MP4 when recording is enabled for that model or plan, and download Marble files when the response includes them.\n"}
